<p>The Pallavas were a prominent kingdom in South India, known for their cultural achievements and military conquests. They were patrons of the arts, and their court was renowned for its poets, musicians, and dancers. The Pallavas also developed a unique system of <strong>temple architecture</strong>, which blended Indian and Southeast Asian styles.</p>
